 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time Complexity:** Dominated by the SDF evaluation for every voxel in the grid ($N^3$) and for every vertex during coloring. Each SDF evaluation iterates over all training cameras. Complexity is roughly $O(N^3 \cdot C + V \cdot C)$, where $N$ is resolution, $C$ is number of cameras, and $V$ is number of vertices [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
-- **Memory Complexity:** $O(N^3)$ for the SDF grid if evaluated densely, or $O(V)$ if evaluated sparsely/chunked. The contraction allows a fixed bounding box regardless of scene size [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
-- **Performance:** Depends heavily on `mesh_res` and number of cameras. High resolution (1024) is computationally expensive [S1, unofficial].
-- **Strengths:** Handles unbounded scenes without manual depth culling or bounding box estimation. Adaptive truncation handles varying Gaussian densities [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
-- **Limitations:** Slow for high resolutions. SDF evaluation is noisy if cameras are sparse [S1, unofficial].
